@title Live view: hold a pushbutton
@area Schematic
@sizes 1366x768
# mouse_down on an Operate button holds it: the row reads "pressed", the
# button is lit and the contactor pulls in; mouse_up lets it go. The press
# used to drop after one frame (the button's id moved when the lines above
# it changed). The harness drops a held press after about 18 frames, so look
# right after the press.
click_text "Open example"
wait 20
key shift+l
wait 20
try click_text "Go to page 2 Control circuit"
wait 20
move 75 397
wait 3
mouse_down 75 397
wait 3
expect "push button · pressed"
expect "pulled in"
shot held
mouse_up 75 397
wait 5
expect_not "push button · pressed"
shot released
